Kai sits on the pickup tailgate. Water trembles in an enamel cup between his knees.

The sharp pattern subsides.

A slower, rounded pulse follows it. The water organizes into a single expanding ring.

Kai stares at the difference.

From the road beyond the gate, the rest of Calabar continues without them.

Ade takes the cup from Kai before he can study the water again.

